# RG35XX RC1 integration specification — Libretro input adapter
# Task: RGJ-RC1-009
# This is an exact-source integration contract, not a BUILD-PASS claim.

OWNER
- org.recompile.freej2me.Libretro remains the binary stdin protocol/parser owner.
- org.recompile.mobile.MobilePlatform remains the MIDP/vendor key dispatch owner.
- org.recompile.mobile.RG35XXInputEngine is the only RG35XX held/repeat state machine.
- Mobile.getMobileKey(code) remains the authoritative frontend-slot -> J2ME key mapping.

REQUIRED LIBRETRO INTEGRATION
1. Import RG35XXInputEngine. Do not create another input class, Timer or repeat thread.
2. Keep the existing 5-byte libretro input protocol and mouse handling unchanged.
3. Validate joypad slot before indexing MobilePlatform.pressedKeys or RG35XXInputEngine state. Invalid slots are ignored, never allowed to throw ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException in the IO thread.
4. For a valid joypad DOWN event, feed the physical/logical frontend slot to RG35XXInputEngine.press(slot, nowMs, sink). The sink converts exactly once with Mobile.getMobileKey(slot) and calls MobilePlatform.keyPressed().
5. For a valid joypad UP event, feed the same slot to RG35XXInputEngine.release(slot, sink); sink converts exactly once and calls MobilePlatform.keyReleased().
6. Do not independently dispatch MobilePlatform.keyPressed/keyReleased beside RG35XXInputEngine, otherwise one physical transition becomes two MIDP transitions.
7. Drive RG35XXInputEngine.update(nowMs, sink) from an already-existing bounded libretro/core update cadence. Do not create a Java repeat worker. Repeat dispatch calls MobilePlatform.keyRepeated(Mobile.getMobileKey(slot)).
8. Keep MobilePlatform.pressedKeys synchronized for upstream compatibility, but it is a compatibility mirror only; it must not become a second repeat generator.
9. Numeric keypad mappings remain owned by Mobile.getMobileKey(). RG35XXInputEngine must not remap numeric keys or phone profiles.
10. Game unload/reset calls RG35XXInputEngine.reset() through RG35XXLifecycle. No held key may leak into the next JAR.

SINK CONTRACT
A single reusable sink instance should be owned by Libretro (not allocated per event):
- keyPressed(slot)  -> MobilePlatform.keyPressed(Mobile.getMobileKey(slot))
- keyReleased(slot) -> MobilePlatform.keyReleased(Mobile.getMobileKey(slot))
- keyRepeated(slot) -> MobilePlatform.keyRepeated(Mobile.getMobileKey(slot))

TIMING
- RG35XXInputEngine owns repeat delay/interval.
- Libretro supplies monotonic-enough milliseconds from an existing clock/update path.
- A delayed update produces at most one repeat for that update; the engine advances nextRepeat to now + interval when behind, preventing repeat storms after stalls.

PRESERVE
- Existing frontend key slot numbering and Mobile.getMobileKey() mapping.
- Existing MobilePlatform MIDP, Vodafone and DoJa state updates.
- Existing Canvas command handling and areKeysSuppressed behavior.
- Mouse rotation/pointer dispatch.
- stdout video IPC and dedicated audio transport are unrelated and unchanged.

BUILD GATE
- Confirm actual libretro update/tick call site for RG35XXInputEngine.update().
- Confirm valid frontend slot range against pressedKeys length and native protocol.
- Compile the consolidated source before marking BUILD-PASS.
